From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SplitPlay <splitplay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 22:47:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] splitplay: keyboard and mouse through the seat's RDP
 connection (input)

New profile field input (docs/contracts/ipc.md), live: "windows" (default,
upstream's SendInput) or "rdp". With "rdp" the worker writes keyboard and
mouse events into the desk's input ring (Global\SplitPlay.InputRing.<desk>,
the MIT contract splitplay/input_ring.h) instead of calling SendInput, and
the seat sends them into the session as RDP input PDUs over its loopback
connection. The session then sees a real remote keyboard and mouse: no
"injected" flag, UAC prompts and Ctrl+Alt+Del work.

- Keys go as scancodes (upstream's VK -> scancode map, MapVirtualKey for
  the rest; Pause as E1 1D 45, Print Screen as E0 37), text as Unicode
  key events, absolute motion in desktop pixels, buttons and wheels with
  the real cursor position (RDP pointer PDUs carry one).
- Relative motion goes over RDP only when the server accepts relative
  mouse PDUs (ring flag SP_INPUT_RING_REL_MOUSE); otherwise it stays on
  SendInput so raw input keeps its deltas.
- Whenever the ring is not usable the event goes to SendInput as before:
  no seat yet, the seat's connection is down (SP_INPUT_RING_READY clear),
  the seat process died, or the ring is full. Input never stops.
- Leaving "rdp" releases whatever is held over RDP (SP_IN_RELEASE_ALL).
- Touch, pen and gamepads are unchanged.

The input thread (input_pool) is the ring's only producer and makes no
system call besides SetEvent; the heartbeat thread opens the ring (every
2 s until it works), watches the seat's process and reports the path as
the metric input: windows, rdp, rdp_mixed (relative motion on SendInput)
or rdp_unavailable, plus input_fallbacks (events that met a full ring).

